# SALES-010: Territory Plans 2025

## 1. Executive Summary

The 2025 Territory Plan outlines the strategic direction for MedSync Health's global sales organization, focusing on maximizing market penetration, driving high-value customer acquisition, and achieving the company's ambitious growth targets. Following a strong FY 2024 performance, which saw total revenue reach **AED 485,100,000** and the customer base expand to **3,930 total organizations** [1], the 2025 plan is designed to capitalize on the momentum in high-growth regions, particularly EMEA and APAC, while solidifying our dominant position in North America.

This plan details the regional revenue targets, resource allocation, key performance indicators (KPIs), and strategic initiatives necessary to achieve a projected 30% year-over-year revenue growth. The strategy is underpinned by a commitment to maintaining a strong LTV:CAC ratio of **10.7** and leveraging our high-performing products, such as MedSync Patient Portal (NPS **75**) [1].

## 2. FY 2024 Performance Review

### 2.1. Revenue by Geographic Region

FY 2024 revenue distribution highlights the critical importance of the North American market, which accounted for 65.0% of total revenue. The 2025 plan is structured to drive accelerated growth in EMEA and APAC to diversify the revenue base and capture emerging market opportunities.

| Region | FY 2024 Revenue (AED) | % of Total Revenue | Q4 2024 Revenue (AED) |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **North America** | 315,315,000 | 65.0% | 85,995,000 |
| **EMEA** | 121,275,000 | 25.0% | 33,075,000 |
| **APAC** | 48,510,000 | 10.0% | 13,230,000 |
| **Total** | **485,100,000** | **100.0%** | **132,300,000** |

### 2.2. Customer Base and Acquisition Metrics

The sales team successfully acquired **890 new customers** in FY 2024, contributing to a net increase of **505** organizations. The focus remains on high-value segments, as reflected in the Average Contract Values (ACV).

| Customer Segment | Total Organizations (End of FY 2024) | Average Contract Value (ACV) | Average Sales Cycle |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Hospitals** | 520 | AED 735,000 | 87 days |
| **Clinics** | 3,200 | AED 73,500 | 34 days |
| **Insurance Providers** | 210 | AED 551,250 | 87 days (aligned with hospitals) |
| **Total** | **3,930** | - | - |

The Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC) for FY 2024 was **AED 152,970** [1]. This metric, combined with the strong Net Revenue Retention (NRR) of **118%** (as detailed in SALES-003: Churn Analysis), validates the efficiency of our current sales and marketing investment [1].

## 3. 2025 Territory Strategy and Goals

### 3.1. Strategic Pillars

1.  **North America (NA) - Deepen Penetration:** Focus on cross-selling and upselling the **MedSync Compliance Suite** (PROD-COMPLIANCE) to the existing base of **520 Hospitals** and **210 Insurance Providers**. Target a 15% increase in ACV for existing accounts.
2.  **EMEA - Accelerated Expansion:** Double the sales headcount in the London and Berlin offices. Target a 40% YoY revenue increase by focusing on the **MedSync Connect** (PROD-CONNECT) platform, which has a strong NPS of **72**.
3.  **APAC - Foundational Growth:** Establish a dedicated sales team in Singapore. Focus on acquiring **Clinics** with the **MedSync Patient Portal** (PROD-PORTAL) due to its shorter **34-day average sales cycle** and high NPS of **75**. Target a 60% YoY revenue increase.

### 3.2. 2025 Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

| KPI | FY 2024 Result | 2025 Target | Strategic Rationale |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Total Revenue** | AED 485,100,000 | AED 630,630,000 | Achieve 30% YoY growth (See FIN-001 for detailed projections) |
| **New Customers Acquired** | 890 | 1,200 | Drive market share, particularly in EMEA and APAC |
| **Average Sales Cycle (Hospitals)** | 87 days | 75 days | Improve sales efficiency through new enablement tools (See OPS-005) |
| **LTV:CAC Ratio** | 10.7 | 11.0 | Maintain high efficiency of sales and marketing spend |
| **Overall Company NPS** | 71 | 75 | Reflects product quality and customer success alignment |

